From 3ff2df5f437247143a76274b21c07547b5b5b7be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:30:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(imu): experimental report deadband to curb movement
 jumpiness; v0.11.71
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SkySafari readout is "jumpy" during movement. Traced to the report path:
in normal fast solving the solve-freshness gate (P1) keeps :GR/:GD on the raw
latest solve, so motion-blurred frames that solve a touch differently each
frame hop the crosshair; in a solve drought the IMU prediction hard-snaps on
every returning solve (_imu_predict_smoothed clears on each ref_t change). Both
are a hard re-anchor to each solve.

Add imu_report_deadband_deg: a position hysteresis on the FINAL reported RA/Dec
(comms _report_radec, applied in J2000 before the JNow precession boundary).
The readout holds steady until the fresh candidate moves more than the deadband,
then advances — suppressing sub-deadband jumps from both sources, at the cost of
deadband-sized steps during a genuine slew (acceptable on a ~13.5 deg finder).

Default 0.25 deg on this experimental branch (so the image exercises it);
0 restores the exact prior behaviour. Live-tunable via solver_params_set
(exposed in solver_params_get too) for on-sky A/B without a restart, and seeded
into shared_cfg. Pure hysteresis helpers (_radec_sep_deg, _apply_report_deadband)
unit-verified: holds sub-deadband jitter, releases on a >deadband move, db=0 is
passthrough.

Experimental, isolated on branch claude/imu-report-deadband-0.11.71 off olive
(v0.11.70) so it can be abandoned cleanly if it proves a dead end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
